		<dc:title id="title">His Royal Nibs</dc:title>
		<meta property="file-as" refines="#title">His Royal Nibs</meta>
		<dc:subject id="subject-1">Ranch life--Fiction</dc:subject>
		<dc:subject id="subject-2">Canada--Fiction</dc:subject>
		<meta property="authority" refines="#subject-1">LCSH</meta>
		<meta property="term" refines="#subject-1">sh2008110351</meta>
		<meta property="authority" refines="#subject-2">LCSH</meta>
		<meta property="term" refines="#subject-2">sh2007100375</meta>
		<meta property="schema:genre">Fiction</meta>
		<meta property="schema:abstract">A young Englishman finds a new purpose in life as a hired hand at a ranch in Canada.</meta>
		<dc:description>
			&lt;p&gt;A young man dubbed “Cheerio” for his English background, clean appearance, and well-kept suit, unexpectedly arrives at the highly regarded O Bar O ranch with one goal in mind: to offer his services as a hired hand, and thus find a new start in life in a foreign land. The ranch’s foreman, Bully Bill, surprised and irritated by the unwelcome stranger, decides to give Cheerio the job after witnessing his cool composure in the presence of a startled herd, preventing the ranch owner’s son from getting injured.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;Cheerio proves his worth at every opportunity and earns the respect, both honest and begrudging, from riders and cowpunchers alike. His hard working day-to-day routine is balanced by his developing friendship with the boy he saved, Sandy McPherson, and the boy’s sister Hilda, for whom Cheerio develops a liking and who has become the subject of Cheerio’s artistic endeavors.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;Everything seems to be going well for Cheerio until an incident at the branding corral brings back uncomfortable memories of his past life. Being deemed a coward and a weak man by his boss and peers, Cheerio grasps at one final chance to redeem himself and achieve his dream: to play a nightly game of chess with Canadian champion and famous rancher P. D. McPherson.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;&lt;i&gt;His Royal Nibs&lt;/i&gt; is a story of resilience, newfound love, and fresh beginnings inspired by &lt;a href="https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/winnifred-eaton-reeve"&gt;Winnifred Eaton Reeve’s&lt;/a&gt; desire to write fiction set in Alberta, Canada after a career spent writing Japanese-themed works under a variety of pseudonyms, the most famous of which being “Onoto Watanna.” &lt;i&gt;His Royal Nibs&lt;/i&gt; would turn out to be her last published novel.&lt;/p&gt;
		</dc:description>
